content.In Patient Treatment:
1. **In Patient Treatment**

We will cover the following Medical Expenses incurred in respect of Hospitalization of the Insured Person during the Policy Period, up to the Annual Sum Insured specified in the Policy Schedule against this Benefit:

- 1. Room Rent up to Twin sharing room (for Annual Sum Insured below \` 10 Lacs and Single private AC room for annual sum insured \` 10L and above);
2. Intensive Care Unit Charges;
3. Qualified Nurse charges;
4. Medical Practitioner’s Fees ;
5. Anaesthesia, blood, oxygen, operation theatre charges, medicines, drugs and consumables (other than those specified in the list of excluded expenses (non-medical) in Annexure I;
6. Surgical appliances and prosthetic devices recommended in writing by the attending Medical Practitioner and that are used intra operatively during a Surgical Procedure;
7. Cost of investigative tests or prescribed diagnostic procedures directly related to the Injury/Illness for which the Insured Person is Hospitalized;

We will consider a claim under this Benefit, subject to the following:

1. The Hospitalization is for Medically Necessary Treatment.
2. The hospitalization warrants inpatient admission in view of active line of treatment.
3. The Hospitalization commences and continues on the written advice of a Medical Practitioner.
4. The Medical Expenses incurred are Reasonable and Customary Charges.
5. If the Insured Person is admitted in a room category/ limit that is higher than the one that is specified in the Policy Schedule/ Product benefit table of this policy, then the Insured Person shall bear a rateable proportion of the total Associated medical expenses (including surcharges or taxes thereon) in the

proportion of the difference between room rent of the entitled room category to the room rent actually incurred

- 1. For the purpose of this cover, “Associated medical expenses” shall include room rent, nursing charges, operation theatre charges, fees of medical practitioner including surgeon/ anaesthetist / specialist within the same hospital where the insured person has been admitted and will not include the cost of pharmacy and consumables, cost of implants, medical devices and cost of diagnostics.
2. Proportionate deductions are not applicable for ICU charges
3. Proportionate deductions shall not be applicable for hospitals which do not follow differential billing or for those expenses in respect of which differential billing is not adopted based on the room category.

1. Expenses associated with automation machine for peritoneal dialysis shall not be payable
2. Any Medical Expenses payable shall not in aggregate exceed the Annual Sum Insured and additional sum insured / cumulative bonus (if any) as specified in the Policy Schedule against this Benefit.

